WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
One shared agent for web chat, telephone and staff dictation. The aim is to help customers and support the team.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Common questions can get answers outside staffed support hours. Several customers can receive help at once, with a clear route to a person.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Reuse approved knowledge for answers, guidance and documentation. Free time for questions that need experience and personal contact.

4
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Chat and telephone help customers. Dictation helps staff prepare a case note.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
An illustrative answer about Wi-Fi calling shows how a customer could receive a clear explanation based on Hektor’s information, with a way to contact support.

6
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Hektor chooses the information: FAQs, guidance, services and terms. Hektor also decides when a person takes over.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:14.000
The illustrative Swedish-language phone conversation answers a general question about Wi-Fi calling. When asked about a subscription, the agent explains that it has no account access and helps the customer reach support. The slide text is translated into English.

8
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:26.000
A proposed support brief gathers the customer’s request, what has been explained and the next step. The example explicitly states that no subscription check was performed.

9
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:38.000
A staff member dictates. Hektor prepares the text. The staff member reviews and corrects it before an approved note is saved through an authorized integration.

10
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Hektor approves information, access and human follow-up. Personal support requires approved integrations, identity checks and appropriate permissions.

11
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:58.000
The agent can explain common questions, guide people and prepare case information. The team retains responsibility for exceptions, sensitive issues, decisions and customer relationships.

12
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:08.000
One shared service can support several staff members. Capacity must be adapted to traffic and agreements; the presentation shows no measured level of automation.

13
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:18.000
More accessible customer service, less recurring work, easier documentation and continued control for Hektor.

14
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:30.000
The commercial direction is one agent at the cost of one support employee, with the potential to automate a whole team’s recurring work. Scope and cost are defined in a quote. The effect has not yet been measured.
